"# Implementation Plan - Restrict Lite Mode (Fix Re-exposed Sidebar categories)

We will fix the bug where switching assets or initial page load re-exposes the 22 tabs (category blocks) and search bar in Lite mode.

## Proposed Changes

### Frontend Components

---

#### [MODIFY] [index.html](file:///c:/Users/Зефирка/StartUp/index.html)

Update the `updateUIContext()` function to check the current `currentProductMode`. If it is `'lite'`, all category blocks (`.category-block`) and the search block should remain hidden, regardless of asset changes.

```javascript
        function updateUIContext() {
            // ...
            const blocks = document.querySelectorAll('.category-block');
            blocks.forEach(block => {
                const subButtons = Array.from(block.querySelectorAll('button'));
                const hasVisible = subButtons.some(b => !b.classList.contains('hidden'));
                if (currentProductMode === 'lite') {
                    block.classList.add('hidden');
                } else {
                    if (hasVisible) {
                        block.classList.remove('hidden');
                    } else {
                        block.classList.add('hidden');
                    }
                }
            });

            const searchBlock = document.getElementById('sidebar-search')?.closest('.relative');
            if (searchBlock) {
                if (currentProductMode === 'lite') {
                    searchBlock.classList.add('hidden');
                } else {
                    searchBlock.classList.remove('hidden');
                }
            }
            // ...
        }
```

